6.Every time the update function runs, a new DoubleTimedValue object is created. This takes more and more space in the heap and makes the garbage collector work harder, which slows the code.
 To fix this, we can change DoubleTimedValue from a record to a regular class, so we can update its values without creating a new object each time. Then, we can create the object once (in the constructor), and in the update method we just change its values using set() method.